<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Amalia Gold in loss, gears for more output.</title>
<headline>Amalia Gold in loss, gears for more output.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-December 31 versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss			2.03    vs 0.37</p>
<p>    Tonnes hoisted		15,286  vs 13,191</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)	    7.18    vs  -</p>
<p>Full name: Amalia Gold Mining and Exploration Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Ore production from underground sources is expected to amount to around 5,000 tonnes a month in early 1997, increasing to around 8,000 tonnes tonnes towards the end of the year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
